{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "את המקום", :translit "et haMakom", :gloss "the place"} {:he "ירושלים", :translit "Yerushalayim", :gloss "Jerusalem"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "את המקום", :b "ירושלים"}], :frame {:text "Abraham was shown the site of the future Temple from afar, identified as the mountain where Isaac would be bound. The Torah calls the destination 'the place' (Genesis 22:4), and this is understood as the Temple Mount in Jerusalem, the permanent site of the altar.", :sources ["Genesis 22:4" "Genesis 22:14" "II Chronicles 3:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מרחק", :translit "merachok", :gloss "from a distance"} {:he "מרחיק", :translit "merachiach", :gloss "was making distant"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling of מרחק read as מרחיק (was making distant), referring to the satan impeding their journey"}], :frame {:text "The satan obstructs the righteous from performing God's will, here by supernaturally stretching the road so the journey seemed endless. This motif of the satan as hinderer appears in rabbinic treatments of the Binding of Isaac.", :sources ["Genesis 22:4"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "את המקום", :a-value 592, :b "ירושלים", :b-value 596, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling of מרחק read as מרחיק (was making distant), referring to the satan impeding their journey", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:07:10.029016945Z", :model "glm-5.2"}